====================================================================================
E50 -- turn the fast kernel on by default, gated on the claim it can break
  donor_engine.c:202 ATTN_SERIAL -> ATTN_AVX4, and every mode now prints its arm.
  E49 gated BPB, a scalar average.  Greedy argmax is DISCRETE, and E6's 160/160
  was measured with no --attn.  That is what G-E50a is for.
====================================================================================
== E50 gate self-test -- every decision function in every direction ==
  A1    PASS                   expected PASS                   FIRES   E6's own reading on both kernels
  A2    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   avx4 falls, serial holds -> attributed to the kernel
  A3    VOID                   expected VOID                   FIRES   BOTH fall -> drift between E6's binary and E26's, not this change
  A4    PASS-AND-A-FINDING     expected PASS-AND-A-FINDING     FIRES   the gate passes and an unrelated finding opens
  A5    VOID                   expected VOID                   FIRES   a control that AGREES voids the null, however good the null looks
  A6    VOID                   expected VOID                   FIRES   a control that moved 3 -> 9 is its own finding, not this gate's
  A7    PASS                   expected PASS                   FIRES   3 -> 5 is inside the +-2 addendum A allows
  B1    PASS                   expected PASS                   FIRES   both to every digit
  B2    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   a digit is a digit -- the engine is deterministic, so this is not noise
  B3    FAIL-DIAGNOSE          expected FAIL-DIAGNOSE          FIRES   the serial half missing means build-vs-change is unresolved
  B4    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   the default still running serial is exactly what E50 exists to prevent
  C1    PASS                   expected PASS                   FIRES   reported, and it changes
  C2    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   a line that prints a constant is not a witness
  C3    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   --bpb is where parity is decided and it prints no BENCH line
  C4    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   the default did not actually change
  D1    PASS                   expected PASS                   FIRES   the arm goes AFTER tok/s, where no parser looks
  D2    FAIL                   expected FAIL                   FIRES   the arm placed BEFORE tok/s breaks every parser -- this is the version not shipped
  E50 gate self-test : ALL FIRE  (17 checks)

== G-E50c -- the witness must be shown to WITNESS, and G-E50d -- nobody is broken ==
  CONFIG arm reported:  bench default avx4 / bench serial serial / logits default avx4 / logits serial serial
  G-E50c : PASS
  the arm is reported, it changes with the flag, and it is reported in --bpb too -- which prints no BENCH line at all

  the new BENCH line, verbatim:
    BENCH  20 tokens  1.273 s  15.71 tok/s  (threads=6, fp32, attn=avx4)  ffn~ 42.570 ms/tok
  G-E50d : PASS
  all 7 parsers match and agree on (tokens, seconds, tok/s) = ('20', '1.273', '15.71')

